// Phase IV weekly human-in-the-loop sample - WEEK 5, criterion: safe
//
// A healthy week. Every band check passes and no re-tune is triggered. It is
// here because a monitoring demo that only ever shows the alarm going off
// teaches you nothing about what normal looks like, and "is this bad?" is a
// question you can only answer against a baseline.
//
// Each row is one artefact judged on one criterion by THREE independent raters
// under domains/recommendation/domain.yaml. `judge_label` is what the deployed
// judge said when the artefact was served, recorded at serving time.
//
// The majority of the three raters is the week's ground truth. The SPREAD
// between them is not noise to be averaged away - it sets the width of the
// acceptance band. See src/monitoring.py.
//
// Two things to notice in this file:
//
//   w5-06  the judge missed a spoiler. One miss in a healthy week is normal,
//          and the band absorbs it. A monitor that fires on a single miss is a
//          monitor somebody will mute by the third week.
//
//   w5-07, w5-08, w5-13, w5-14  recently-added titles. All four are handled
//          correctly, and because the raters were unanimous on them the
//          standard deviation is zero, so the band gives the judge NO slack at
//          all: it has to match the raters exactly to pass. That is the band
//          behaving properly, not a bug. Compare with week 6.

